From: Hikari Linux Project <hikari-linux@localhost>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 07:45:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: qcom: stop watchdog on reboot

The Qualcomm watchdog core keeps an inherited running watchdog alive after
probe.  During a slow kexec shutdown the watchdog core's keepalive worker
stops, but qcom-wdt leaves the hardware enabled.  On MSM8x60 this allows the
30-second bark to fire as PPI 3 (Linux IRQ 19) while the old kernel is still
shutting down, producing an unhandled interrupt storm that prevents kexec.

Ask the watchdog core to stop the hardware from its reboot notifier.  The
driver already provides a stop operation, and its separate restart handler
will still arm the short bite used for an actual hardware restart.
---
 drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
@@ -327,6 +327,7 @@ static int qcom_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &wdt->wdd.status);
 	}
 
+	watchdog_stop_on_reboot(&wdt->wdd);
 	ret = devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, &wdt->wdd);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-- 
2.47.3
